  "provenance": "Source-authored SAFE controls for host-hardened semantic qualification, separated from v1/v2 and the original corpus. Distinct Salesforce CLI diagnostic reads and Slack Canvas section/metadata reads are grouped with three equivalent shell variants per operation across TRAIN, VALIDATION, and TEST. Labels follow operation-policy-v1: metadata, status, canvases.sections.lookup (read over POST), and files.list?types=canvas (read over GET) make no durable write. Salesforce org observations are independently authored as DevOrg sandbox; Slack requests contain only an environment-token expansion and no Salesforce org observation. Source references: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/salesforce-cli-reference/guide/cli_reference_agent_test_list.html ; https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/salesforce-cli-reference/guide/cli_reference_agent_adl_list.html ; https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/salesforce-cli-reference/guide/cli_reference_agent_adl_status.html ; https://docs.slack.dev/reference/methods/canvases.sections.lookup/ ; https://docs.slack.dev/surfaces/canvases/ . TEST cases were authored from these sources without reading the original held-out corpus or using model predictions. Human label review is still pending.",
